  "term": "flooding",
  "definition": "Flooding is the overflow of water in urban areas, often linked to extreme rainfall or rivers, that can damage infrastructure and disrupt how communities move people and goods. In a social context, it is described as a growing environmental stressor that threatens accessibility, economic activity, and community resilience.",
